## Context
The 2026-06-11 prose review panel (pre-arXiv) found the manuscript's hand-typed
numbers stale against the committed generated artifacts:
- Annex screen-validation section vs `report/inputs/generated/tab_screen_validation_within_model.csv`:
  prose τ=+0.215 vs CSV 0.321; 65/42 concordant/discordant pairs vs 70/36;
  status τ +0.312 vs 0.419; 10/14 vs 11/14 models; binary gap +0.162 vs 0.190;
  vetoed/surviving means 0.146/0.481 vs 0.112/0.350.
- Exp1 cost: prose $2.85 vs macro `\CensusCostTotal{6.21}`.
- Fusion: best-single F1 0.679 vs CSV 0.673; fusion CSV scored against
  n_reference=173 not 177 — undisclosed in prose (disclose or regenerate).

Author decision (2026-06-11): fix the class, not the instances. Every empirical
number in the manuscript goes through a macro, with a single global
`macros.tex` generated by the pipeline and wired into the Makefile DAG.
This is the macro-mechanism extension of the existing rule "derive prose from
generated artifacts, never from agent enumeration" (.claude/rules/workflow.md).

Blocked by 0524: the macro inclusion mechanism depends on whether the
manuscript stays pandoc (`main.md`, raw-LaTeX `\input`) or converts to LaTeX.
Design the macros file once 0524's build choice is recorded.

## Relevant files
- `slides/manuscript/main.md` — manuscript source (all hand-typed empirical numbers)
- `report/inputs/generated/`, `slides/inputs/generated/` — existing per-table artifacts and macros
- `slides/inputs/generated/macros_census.tex` — existing partial macros precedent
- `slides/Makefile` — wire `macros.tex` as a first-class artifact in the DAG
- `src/aedist/` — table/figure scripts to extend with macro emission
- `.claude/rules/writing.md` — record the macros house rule once shipped

## Actions
1. Inventory every empirical literal in the manuscript (counts, F1, τ, $, %, n).
2. Extend the generating scripts to emit one consolidated `macros.tex`
   (one source of truth; per-script fragments concatenated by a Make rule is fine).
3. Replace literals with macro references; regenerate so prose matches artifacts
   (this closes the stale-numbers findings above by construction).
4. Wire `macros.tex` into the Makefile: manuscript target depends on it.

## Folded scope: 0501 — reconcile prose to the v2.4 (177) reference

Closed ticket 0501 lands here (folded 2026-06-11): #906 (ticket 0497) moved the
reference to v2.4 = 177 plants but deferred the prose sync, so `main.md` still
carries the v2.1 = 173 vintage. NOT a find-replace (v2.2/v2.3 skipped — fuel
split and status breakdowns moved too); every value re-derived from the
committed artifact, which is exactly what the macro pass does. Author decision
2026-06-09: ship the preprint at 177. Concretely, the macro inventory (action 1)
must cover at least:

1. 18× "173[-plant]" prose/caption mentions → count macro from `reference_plant_count()`.
2. Annex B fuel split `coal (81) and gas/gas-oil (92)` → recompute from
   `data/reference/vietnam_thermal_plants_v2_classified.csv`.
3. §7 difficulty table total row (`**173** / 100.0% / 26.2%`) + status-group
   rows → re-derive from the generating script's committed artifact.
4. §6 fusion secondary numbers (`166 candidates`, recall 0.633/0.262/0.391/0.671,
   F1 0.659/0.689, "2.4×") → re-derive from the fusion sweep artifact
   (#906 updated only the §4 macros).
5. Figure 7 caption ("173 reference plants") — the figure already renders 177 columns.

Inherited notes from 0501: line-90 attribute accuracies (province 0.61→0.89)
stay deferred to 0502 (scoring change, not a 177 effect). 0494 (Wikipedia
recall bar) depends on this count sync — unblocked when this ticket closes.

## Test
- Adherence test: the manuscript source contains no bare empirical literal
  from a known generated artifact (re-derive a sample of guarded numbers from
  the CSVs via independent parse, assert the macro values match).
- From 0501 (write FIRST, must fail on current source): every reference-count
  mention equals `reference_plant_count()`; stale literals ("173-plant",
  "173 reference", …) absent — `tests/test_manuscript_reference_count.py`,
  `@pytest.mark.adherence` (0501 body in tickets/closed/ has a draft against
  `main.md`; target the post-0524 `.tex` source).

## Invariants
- `make -C slides manuscript/main.pdf` builds clean-room (`make -B -n` honest).
- Tectonic include trap (.claude/rules/writing.md): a new include file is
  acceptable here because a script regenerates it on every build.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Global generated `macros.tex` exists, Makefile-wired, regenerated by pipeline.
- [ ] No hand-typed empirical number in manuscript prose; all via macros.
- [ ] All review-listed stale numbers now correct (match committed artifacts).
- [ ] Fusion n_reference (173 vs 177) either regenerated to 177 or disclosed in prose.
- [ ] Folded 0501 scope: no 173-vintage reference-count literal survives; fuel
      split, difficulty table, §6 fusion numbers, Figure 7 caption all match
      their committed artifacts (cite artifact + value in the PR).
- [ ] `tests/test_manuscript_reference_count.py` exists and passes (failed first).
- [ ] Adherence test guards the class.
